# Weatherhaven Special Forces

## Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS v4 (`src/app/globals.css` with `@import "tailwindcss"`)
- Supabase (auth + data), Resend (email), Three.js, Leaflet
- Vitest for unit tests in `src/**/*.test.ts`

## Layout

- Routes and pages: `src/app/`
- Shared UI: `src/components/`
- Server utilities and data: `src/lib/`
- Import alias: `@/*` → `src/*`
- Supabase SQL: `supabase/`
- Env template: `.env.example` (never commit `.env.local`)

## Product areas

- Marketing: `/`, `/capabilities`, `/configurable-solutions`, `/contact`, etc.
- SOF portal: `/sof-solutions/*` (login, request-access, `/sof-solutions/secure/*`)
- Admin dashboard: `/admin`
- 3D / map tools: mission-solution-builder, tactical-map (redirects in `next.config.ts`)

## Conventions

- After implementation changes: run `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build` before finishing.
- Marketing pages must not cause horizontal page scroll; use `overflow-x-hidden` on layouts and avoid `overflow-x-auto` on marketing UI except inside contained tables.
- Lead flow uses `access_requests` as the single source of truth (`POST /api/request-access`).
- See `docs/PRODUCTION.md` for env vars and deploy checklist; `AGENTS.md` for commit/push workflow when the user allows it.
